      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Veloce Model X Side-Impact Test - Post-Simulation Documentation:\n\nDuring the side-impact test at 64km/h, we have observed significant test outcomes; specifically, there was vehicle intrusion on the driver side amounting to 15cm. Evidence of a failure was noted as the steering column underwent a structural snap at approximately 0.4 seconds into the event. The airbag system demonstrated a deficiency by deploying approximately 22 milliseconds after impact, which conflicts with standard safety mechanisms. The seatbelt pretensioner functioned correctly; however, it did not prevent contact between the occupant and the chest, suggesting that it deployed too slowly and did not provide the intended seatbelt restraint protection. Following the test, we confirmed the cabin's integrity was compromised, particularly within the footwell area. Current action plans include a thorough investigation of the airbag and seatbelt pretensioner systems to prevent recurrence and enhance occupant safety in future models.",
